    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dr. Pepper's Liquid Ice Blend is an over-the-counter product that combines alcohol and menthol crystals to provide temporary relief for nerve pain. It works by numbing the skin and reducing irritation. Be sure to follow the instructions carefully to avoid any adverse effects.\n\nWhile it's understandable to want immediate relief, care must be taken with dosage. The safe dose of Tylenol (acetaminophen) as per FDA guidelines is 325-650mg every 4 hours, with a maximum daily dose of 3000mg for most adults. If you'd like to spread it out over 12 hours, you may aim for taking 500mg to 650mg each, but do so with extreme caution. You should also avoid taking it if you have potentially liver-compromising conditions, consume alcohol, or are on other medications that can affect the liver.\n\nIf pain management is critical for you, speak to a pharmacist for safe combinations of remedies that are legally available besides Tylenol. It's still recommended to seek professional medical advice for safe and effective treatment, as storing doses beyond recommended intervals can lead to dangerous consequences. Applying a cold compress could also provide some temporary relief. Remember, it's important not to push your body's limits with medication without guidance.",
